    "q-241885": {
      "dom_id": "step-q241885",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =0.64$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha =1.25$, where $\\theta $ and $\\alpha $ are acute angles measured in degrees, then $\\theta +\\alpha $ in degrees to one decimal place is{{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\theta $ and $\\alpha $ we use $arccos$ and $arctan$ respectively. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =0.64 \\\\ \\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0.64) \\\\ \\theta  & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0.64)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha  & =1.25 \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha ) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1.25) \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1.25).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta +\\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0.64)+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1.25) \\\\  & =(50.208\\,1…)^{∘}+(51.340\\,1…)^{∘} \\\\  & =(101.548\\,2…)^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{101.5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
